      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg three times daily). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO two or three times daily**, if you're starting or titrating.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
